{
  "_about": "Hand-authored synthetic dataset for the Pass 2 evaluation contract (schema v2). It contains NO real legislation and NO human judgments -- every 'adjudicator' is 'synthetic'. Its job is to prove, before any human labels anything, that the frozen schema can produce all five promised metrics over populations whose truth is ADEQUATE for each metric, and that every guard actually excludes. Rounds 1-2 shapes: clean one-to-one, global none, one-to-many with a retrieval gap, a candidate miss found only by browsing, a ranking miss, an assignment collision with one winner and one loser, a suggestion-list-only positive, an uncertain, and a challenge-stratum failure. Round 3 adversarial shapes: a region-only NONE that must not reach diff correctness, a cross-region counterpart the escalation caught, a suggestion-list NONE, and two distinct nodes sharing body text (the boilerplate case, measured in 33% of real documents) in both the wrong-node and right-node directions.",
  "schema_version": "pass2-anchor-v2",
